{
	"_about": "Leatherworking 1-300: the curated route the profession guide is generated from (tools/lib/professions/route.js; rules: docs/forge/professions.md, \"Route files\"). Every recipe, count, trainer, vendor and pattern seller is checked against data/forever when the guide is built.",
	"profession": "Leatherworking",
	"intro": [
		"Leatherworking cures hides and stitches leather into armour and armour kits. Skinning is its partner: leather is most of what the route costs, and every leather on it is one you can skin yourself. Hides are a rare find when skinning, so the route gets them from the Auction House (the ones you skin count too); the salt, threads and dyes come from vendors.",
		"Ranks: Apprentice at any level from any Leatherworking trainer (the first trainer teaches recipes only up to 50); Journeyman from level 10 at the city trainers, who teach the recipes up to 150; Expert from level 20 (50s) at Telonis in Darnassus or Una in Thunder Bluff; Artisan from level 35 at Drakk Stonehand in Aerie Peak or Hahrana Ironhide in Camp Mojache.",
		"Two patterns come from vendors: Wicked Leather Gauntlets (Leonard Porter in the Western Plaguelands, Werg Thickblade in Tirisfal Glades) and Runic Leather Headband (Jase Farlane at Light's Hope Chapel). Patterns that need a Tanning Rack or a Sewing Machine are left out: no town has either."
	],
